      56.66,
      118.64,
      522.69,
      172.25
    ],
    "text": "Bulletin No: 07 MSW/26/10/27/01 COLOR: Red Warning for strong winds and rough seas.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.039999961853027,
      9.960000038146973,
      12.0,
      15.960000038146973
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.66,
      172.82,
      378.74,
      217.58
    ],
    "text": "Issued by the Natural Hazards Early Warning Centre Issued at 08.00 a.m. 27 October 2026, valid for the next 12 hours.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold",
      "Iskoola Pota"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      0.9599999785423279,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      220.61,
      518.33,
      234.65
    ],
    "text": "For the Bay of Bengal and deep and shallow sea areas around the island.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.66,
      237.26,
      553.97,
      418.97
    ],
    "text": "Take Action! For Multiday Boats The Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cArnab\u201d over West central Bay of Bengal intensified into a \u2018Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\u2019 and lay centered at 02.30 a.m. of today, the 27th October, 2026 over the near latitude 15.9\u00b0N and longitude 85.4\u00b0E about 890 km to the north-east of Kankasanthurai. It is very likely to continue to move west-northwestwards till 05.30 p.m. of 27th October and thereafter, it is very likely to move northwestwards and cross the Indian land through Andhra Pradesh coast as a very severe cyclonic storm by 11.30 a.m. of 28th October, 2026.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0,
      14.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.66,
      422.39,
      554.1,
      527.11
    ],
    "text": "Although this system is not expected to have a direct impact on Sri Lanka, the showery condition over the southwestern parts of the island is expected continue today, as the wind flow associated with the system extends across the island. Wind speeds in the sea areas marked under the \u201cWarning\u201d category may increase to 80-140 kmph at times, heavy thundershowers can occur, the wave height may increase about (3.0 \u2013 4.0) meters in the mentioned sea areas and the sea conditions in these areas will become very rough.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.039999961853027,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.66,
      546.31,
      555.67,
      872.64
    ],
    "text": "Therefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the sea areas bounded by 10N to 20N latitude and 80E to 95E longitude until further notice. Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move away from the affected sea areas.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      56.66,
      971.4,
      555.46,
      993.45
    ],
    "text": "2",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      9.0,
      11.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      56.66,
      120.14,
      553.54,
      165.74
    ],
    "text": "Naval and fishing communities engaging the activities over this sea area are advised to be vigilant and be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the department of meteorology in this regards.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
